RESY is released under the MIT licence (see LICENSE), except for the
third-party data listed below, which keep their own licences and copyright
notices. Each entry names the files, their source, the licence and the
attribution the provider asks for.


Expert system
-------------

inst/extdata/classifications/EUNIS/2025-10-03/expert.json.xz
  EUNIS-ESy expert system, version 2025-10-03 (Zenodo,
  https://zenodo.org/records/16895007), in RESY's JSON format.
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
  Cite: Chytrý, M. et al. (2020) EUNIS Habitat Classification: expert system,
  characteristic species combinations and distribution maps of European
  habitats. Applied Vegetation Science. https://doi.org/10.1111/avsc.12519,
  version 2025-10-03.


Geographic data (data/)
-----------------------

data/ecoregions2017_epsg25832.rda
  RESOLVE Ecoregions 2017, European subset, reprojected to EPSG:25832.
  Licence: CC BY 4.0 (https://ecoregions.appspot.com).
  Cite: Dinerstein, E. et al. (2017) An ecoregion-based approach to protecting
  half the terrestrial realm. BioScience 67.
  https://doi.org/10.1093/biosci/bix014

data/coastline_regions_epsg25832.rda
  Regional seas around Europe (Marine Strategy Framework Directive regions),
  European Environment Agency, reprojected to EPSG:25832.
  Licence: CC BY 4.0, EEA reuse policy (https://www.eea.europa.eu/en/legal-notice).
  Source: European Environment Agency (EEA).

data/europe_resolution_1_epsg25832.rda
data/europe_resolution_60_epsg25832.rda
  NUTS level 0 boundaries, 1:1 million and 1:60 million, Eurostat GISCO,
  reprojected to EPSG:25832.
  Terms: Eurostat GISCO copyright notice for administrative units
  (https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/gisco/geodata/statistical-units).
  © EuroGeographics for the administrative boundaries.

data/dunes_bohn_500mbuffer_epsg25832.rda
  Coastal vegetation (formation P) of the Map of the Natural Vegetation of
  Europe, buffered by 500 m, reprojected to EPSG:25832.
  Cite: Bohn, U. et al. Map of the Natural Vegetation of Europe. Federal
  Agency for Nature Conservation (BfN).


Example data (inst/extdata/)
----------------------------

inst/extdata/data_example_altitude.tif
  Cropped from EuroDEM (https://www.mapsforeurope.org/datasets/euro-dem).
  Licence: EuroGeographics Open Data Licence
  (https://www.mapsforeurope.org/licence).
  This dataset includes Intellectual Property from European National Mapping
  and Cadastral Authorities and is licensed on behalf of these by
  EuroGeographics. Original dataset is available for free at
  https://www.mapsforeurope.org. Terms of the licence available at
  https://www.mapsforeurope.org/licence.

inst/extdata/data_example_species.csv
inst/extdata/data_example_sites.csv
  Source: <not found>
  Licence: <not found>

inst/extdata/eunis_2021_names.csv
  Source: the names follow the EEA EUNIS habitat type hierarchical view
  (marine version 2022, terrestrial version 2021),
  https://eunis.eea.europa.eu/habitats-code-browser-revised.jsp. The types
  the EEA list does not hold follow Chytrý et al. (2020), EUNIS Habitat
  Classification: Expert system, characteristic species combinations and
  distribution maps of European habitats, Applied Vegetation Science (N23,
  N24, Q32 and others), and Schaminée et al. (2022), Support to EUNIS habitat
  classification (Pa to Pj).
  Licence: <not found>


Species-name synonym table (inst/extdata/)
------------------------------------------

inst/extdata/esy_synonym_layer.csv.xz
  Built by data-raw/build_synonyms.R from the synonym lists of the taxonomic
  backbones below (versions in inst/extdata/esy_synonym_layer_backbones.csv).

  Euro+Med PlantBase (https://europlusmed.org).
    Licence: CC BY-SA 3.0 Unported (notice on the Euro+Med taxon pages,
    https://ww2.bgbm.org/EuroPlusMed/).
    Cite: Euro+Med 2006+ [continuously updated]: Euro+Med PlantBase - the
    information resource for Euro-Mediterranean plant diversity. Published at
    http://www.europlusmed.org
  World Flora Online (WFO) taxonomic backbone.
    Licence: CC0 1.0 (https://www.worldfloraonline.org/downloadData).
    Cite: WFO (2026): World Flora Online. Version 2026.06. Published on the
    Internet; http://www.worldfloraonline.org.
  GBIF Backbone Taxonomy.
    Licence: CC BY 4.0.
    Cite: GBIF Secretariat (2023). GBIF Backbone Taxonomy. Checklist dataset
    https://doi.org/10.15468/39omei
  Catalogue of Life (COL).
    Licence: CC BY (https://api.checklistbank.org/dataset/3LR).
    Cite: Catalogue of Life checklist, version 2026.09.
  Integrated Taxonomic Information System (ITIS).
    Licence: CC0 (https://www.itis.gov/citation.html).
    Retrieved from the Integrated Taxonomic Information System (ITIS) on-line
    database, www.itis.gov, CC0. https://doi.org/10.5066/F7KH0KBK
  NCBI Taxonomy.
    National Library of Medicine (NLM) is acknowledged as the source.
